Output ONLY valid JSON.

ALLOWED EVENTS: ["Diagnosis", "Discharge", "Examination", "Expert Examination", "Register at ER", "Register at FD", "Thorough Examination", "Treatment", "Treatment successful", "Treatment unsuccessful"]
ALLOWED OBJECTS: ["Person"]
OBJECT ATTRIBUTES:
  Person: overallProtected (String: 0, 1), isGermanspeaking (String: 0, 1), isPrivate_insurance (String: 0, 1), isUnderlying_condition (String: 0, 1), Age (String), isGender (String: 0, 1), isCitizen (String: 0, 1), Case (String), sumBoolDiscrFactors (String: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5), numOcc_RegisteratER (String: 0, 1), numOcc_ExpertExamination (String: 0, 1), numOcc_Diagnosis (String: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6), numOcc_Treatment (String: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6), numOcc_Treatmentsuccessful (String: 0, 1), numOcc_Discharge (String: 1), numOcc_RegisteratFD (String: 0, 1), numOcc_ThoroughExamination (String: 0, 1), numOcc_Examination (String: 0, 1), numOcc_Treatmentunsuccessful (String: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5), reworkedActivities (String: 0, 11, 14, 2, 5, 8), throughputTime (Float)
EVENT-TO-OBJECT RELATIONS (only these event/object pairs are linked):
  Diagnosis -> Person
  Discharge -> Person
  Examination -> Person
  Expert Examination -> Person
  Register at ER -> Person
  Register at FD -> Person
  Thorough Examination -> Person
  Treatment -> Person
  Treatment successful -> Person
  Treatment unsuccessful -> Person
Use ONLY the relations listed above. If two entities are not directly related, connect them through an intermediary that is.

